 [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n*[[Cookbook:Margarine|Margarine]] or rapeseed/other vegetable [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|oil]]\n*[[Cookbook:Soy sauce|Soy sauce]] (optional)\n*[[Cookbook:Mustard|Mustard]] (optional)\n*[[Cookbook:Ketchup|Ketchup]] (optional)\n*[[Cookbook:Garlic|Garlic]] (optional)\n*[[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]] (optional)\n*[[Cookbook:Onion|Onions]] (optional)\n*[[Cookbook:Thyme|Thyme]] (optional)\n*Seasoning mix (corn flour, salt, chili, onion, garlic, paprika; e.g. Mexican taco seasoning mix)\n\n==Procedure==\n# Mash the rice. Mix in the flour, margarine, and some water until you get a homogeneous mass.\n# Mix in the optional ingredients to taste. You can also try to just add your favorite herbs and no other ingredients.\n# Let rest to absorb the flavor of the herbs.\n\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[de:Kochbuch/ Brotaufstrich aus Reis und Weizen]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ketchup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]\n[[Category:Recipes using prepared mustard]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Rice Wheat Spread","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"400 g cooked rice","sourceText":"400 g cooked rice","amountText":"400 g cooked rice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"150 g wheat flour","sourceText":"150 g wheat flour","amountText":"150 g wheat flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Margarine or rapeseed/other vegetable oil","sourceText":"Margarine or rapeseed/other vegetable oil","amountText":"Margarine or rapeseed/other vegetable oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"Soy sauce (optional)","sourceText":"Soy sauce (optional)","amountText":"Soy sauce (optional)","amount":null,"unit":